    "id": 9253,
    "question": "It's late at night and a valuation you are working on with another analyst is not producing the expected results. What do you do?",
    "answer": "Reported in RBC Interview First round First and foremost, maintain integrity. Never force the numbers to fit expectations. Work systematically with your peer to troubleshoot. Double-check all inputs for errors, review key assumptions for reasonableness, and trace the formulas in the model to find any mechanical mistakes. Sense-check the results. Compare the output to other valuation methodologies (e.g., if the DCF is off, how does it compare to the Comps?). If the discrepancy persists after thorough checking, document the steps taken and the potential issues identified. Prepare a concise summary and flag it for your associate or VP first thing in the morning, clearly explaining the issue and the diligence performed.",
    "topic": "General Banking Knowledge",
    "difficulty": "Basic",
    "type": "behavioral",
    "firms": [
      "RBC"
    ]
